statement:
Prove that twelve circles of equal radius can be placed on a sphere with the following tangencies, and no others. Label them $A_i,B_i,C_i$ for $i=1,2,3,4$, reading indices modulo $4$:

- $A_i$ touches $A_{i-1},A_{i+1},B_{i-1},B_i,C_i$;
- $B_i$ touches $A_i,A_{i+1},C_i,C_{i+1}$;
- $C_i$ touches $A_i,B_{i-1},B_i$.

Thus four circles each touch five others, four each touch four, and four each touch three.
